# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <!-- `ignore` matches whole event names only -->
  <VueComponent @customEventName="onEvent" />
  <!-- `ignoreTags` matches tag names exactly -->
  <IgnoredComponentTwo @otherEvent="onEvent" />
</template>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.vue:4:18 lint/nursery/useVueConsistentEventHyphenation  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i The event name customEventName isn't hyphenated.
  
    2 │ <template>
    3 │   <!-- `ignore` matches whole event names only -->
  > 4 │   <VueComponent @customEventName="onEvent" />
      │                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    5 │   <!-- `ignoreTags` matches tag names exactly -->
    6 │   <IgnoredComponentTwo @otherEvent="onEvent" />
  
  i Vue matches event listeners regardless of their casing, so mixing camelCase and kebab-case event names makes templates inconsistent.
  
  i This project requires hyphenated (kebab-case) event names.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Rename the event to custom-event-name.
  
    2 2 │   <template>
    3 3 │     <!-- `ignore` matches whole event names only -->
    4   │ - ··<VueComponent·@customEventName="onEvent"·/>
      4 │ + ··<VueComponent·@custom-event-name="onEvent"·/>
    5 5 │     <!-- `ignoreTags` matches tag names exactly -->
    6 6 │     <IgnoredComponentTwo @otherEvent="onEvent" />
  

```

